---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config/site';
---
<Legal
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What this site stores, why, and how to ask to see or delete it."
  altPath="/privacidade/"
  back={SITE.name}
>
  <p>
    This site (<strong>{SITE.url}</strong>) has no advertising or visit tracking — no Google
    Analytics, no pixels, no third-party cookies. What follows is only what the site's own features
    need in order to work.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you use the contact form, your email and message are sent to me by email (via
    <a href="https://resend.com">Resend</a>) and are not stored on the server.
  </p>

  <h2>Blog subscription</h2>
  <p>
    I store your email, chosen language, and subscription status, in a simple list on the server.
    You can leave whenever you want, from the link in any email I send you — I never share or sell
    this list.
  </p>

  <h2>Signing in (Calendar and comments)</h2>
  <p>There are two ways to sign in, and both land in the same place — a session identified only by your email:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A code by email:</strong> there is no password to store.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sign in with Google:</strong> Google confirms the inbox is yours and hands me back your
      email — nothing else. I do not request or store your name, photo, or any other profile data.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    While you are signed in, a cookie stores your email in signed form. If you book a conversation on
    the Calendar, I store the time, the subject, and any note you write, so I can honour it and email
    you about it.
  </p>

  <h2>Messages (the assistant)</h2>
  <p>
    Conversations with the site's assistant are stored — who started them (your email, if you were
    signed in; otherwise an anonymous fingerprint of your visit) and the text of each message — so I
    can read the context of anyone who has talked to me before. This is the one exception to the rest
    of this site: everywhere else, what you type does not stay stored once your request is done.
  </p>
  <p>
    Text you send to the assistant is also processed by a language model, through
    <a href="https://openrouter.ai">OpenRouter</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Comments and reactions on writing</h2>
  <p>
    A comment shows your name and the text you wrote, publicly, underneath the post. Your email is
    stored but <strong>never shown to anyone else</strong> — it exists only so I can reply, if that
    makes sense. A reaction (👍 ❤️ 💡) shows nothing about you, only the total count per post.
  </p>

  <h2>A fingerprint of your visit</h2>
  <p>
    To prevent abuse (bots, bulk submissions), the server stores a fingerprint of your visit — never
    your raw IP address, always a signature (HMAC) that changes on every server restart and cannot be
    reversed back to the original IP. It is not shared, not sold, and disappears on its own.
  </p>

  <h2>Stocks</h2>
  <p>
    Your symbol list in the Stocks app stays only on your device (browser <code>localStorage</code>)
    — it never reaches the server. Quotes come from Yahoo Finance.
  </p>

  <h2>Where all of this lives</h2>
  <p>
    The data described above lives on a server in Europe, and is never sold or shared with anyone
    beyond the providers already named (Resend, OpenRouter, Google, Yahoo Finance), each only with
    what it needs for its own role.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see, correct, or delete what this site stores about you — write to
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. I answer myself, directly; there is no support
    team.
  </p>

  <p><em>Last updated: September 2026.</em></p>
</Legal>
